.SH NAME
coverage\-audit \- audit published permit\-request coverage against local parcels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coverage\-audit [\-parcels VALUE] [\-published VALUE] [\-checkpoint VALUE] [\-batch\-size VALUE] [\-plans VALUE] [\-as\-of VALUE] [\-clean\-out VALUE] [\-previous VALUE] [\-json VALUE] [\-mcp VALUE]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Reads local files only and compares the published permit\-request feed against the local parcels dataset, reporting batch coverage and cursor consistency. Cursor progress is not verified query success. With \-clean\-out it writes a separate normalized dataset and never overwrites the input. With \-mcp it serves read\-only MCP over stdio.
